WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.167
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.634
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.901
Well, guys,
here's something to celebrate.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:11.467
Today is the last day
of dry January.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.767
What an accomplishment.

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.701
I can't believe
we all went an entire month

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:18.868
lying to each other.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.267
Let's get to some news here.
Today, President Biden

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.434
was here in New York City
to talk about the funding

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.534
for his infrastructure law.

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.601
Yeah, Biden's speech was great
because for 20 minutes,

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.100
the city that never sleeps
got a quick little snooze.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.534
Yeah, this week,
Biden's been touring the country

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.434
to talk about
his infrastructure plan.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.501
Meanwhile, people are talking
about all these videos

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.234
that Donald Trump Jr.
keeps releasing

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:47.000
where he can't stop
using air quotes.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.200
[ Laughter ]
You see this?

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.767
So, we decided
to combine the two.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.901
So, here's Joe Biden's head
on Don Jr.'s body.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.067
Enjoy.

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.234
-But, folks, look,
I made a thousand trips

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:57.667
through this tunnel,
so I've been through this tunnel

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.300
a thousand times.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.267
And, you know,
when folks talk about

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:04.534
how badly the Baltimore Tunnel
needs an upgrade,

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:07.400
you don't need me to tell you.
I've been there.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.767
-Yeah.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:14.734
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:16.501
I -- I also, I feel like --
is it me?

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.601
I feel like Biden's voice is
kind of sounding like

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.901
a Jennifer Coolidge impression.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.834
Like, "You don't need me
to tell you.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:26.100
Oh, my God."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.501
"I feel the Republicans
are trying to murder me."

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.033
"I can go
for a hot tub real bad."

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.334
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:36.901
Here's some big news.
On May 11th, President Biden

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:40.501
is going to end the COVID
public-health emergency.

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:41.968
I'm pretty sure the public

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.300
ended the health emergency
a while ago.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.300
Today, I saw a guy
open a Starbucks bathroom

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.167
with his tongue.
I go, "I think it's over."

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Hey!

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:52.834
Hey!
-Listen to this.

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:55.300
According to researchers,
American democracy

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.100
could be failing 'cause elected
officials are getting too old.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.901
Well, a few politicians
in Washington

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:03.000
were quick to respond about them
being too old.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.667
First up,
President Biden said...

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:08.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.234
And Bernie Sanders said...

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.834
And finally,
this Senator said...

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:21.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.968
No cap.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.968
I saw that former president
Trump is suing Bob Woodward

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:29.834
for releasing interview
recordings that Trump says

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:33.200
that he never agreed could be
shared with the public.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.767
And if you listen,
you can actually tell why

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:35.834
Trump didn't want these
released.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.000
Check these out.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.667
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah, that's two words.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.834
[ Applause ]

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.868
One word.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.133
Did you guys see this?
Amid all the controversy,

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:18.934
Congressman George Santos said
that he is temporarily

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:22.767
stepping down from his House
committee assignments.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:23.901
-Yeah!
[ Scattered applause ]

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.467
In a statement, Santos said...

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.267
Then he said...

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:34.400
Then he said...

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:39.534
And finally, he said...

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:49.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:52.267
I didn't know that.

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.400
Well, some movie news.
Today, Warner Bros. announced

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.767
that "The Batman II,"
starring Robert Pattinson,

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:59.634
will be released
in October of 2025.

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:03.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.801
Not to be outdone,
Marvel just announced

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.367
that there's eight new movies
coming out tomorrow,

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:10.033
and you have to see them all.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.033
Well, guys, the weather
has been crazy this winter.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.868
Some places have a ton of snow,
others haven't gotten any.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.434
But one thing's for sure,
when you're watching

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.100
a weather report,
you just want to skip

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.167
the boring parts and get right
to the important stuff.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:21.868
Well, it turns out you can.

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:23.200
For instance,
if you're watching a report,

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.400
you can skip this part.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.100
-Good morning.
Well, obviously,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.767
we're getting a nice break
from the rain.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.801
-Yeah, and you go
right to this part.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.834
-This is essentially now
a part of the Passaic River

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:33.934
in this neighborhood.
-Wait a second.

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:36.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:38.801
-"Wait.
What are you guys doing?"

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:41.100
-"What the...?"

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.434
Maybe it was two Jesuses.
-Here's another example.

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:44.868
You can skip this part.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.567
-Hey, Michael, I hear you're
slipping and sliding out there

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:48.434
on the Weather Deck.
-Took a look at this

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:49.834
wide view here
of the Weather Deck.

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.868
-Yeah, and you can go
right to this part.

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:53.601
-It's just completely
glazed over.

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:54.934
And...

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.334
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my goodness.

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.334
That did not feel good.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.067
-Ooh, ooh.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.334
-Ow.
-That's right.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.067
You can --
You can skip this part.

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:05.701
-58 right now
in the Twin Cities.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.167
It's a comfortable
Tuesday night.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.767
46 in Hinckley.
57 in Marshall.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.100
-And go right to this.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.868
-In Winona --
Ooh, that's funky.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:20.067
You guys want
one Jennifer or two Jennifers?

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:23.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:26.400
-Yeah, here's a final example.
You can skip this part.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.334
-All right.
So, I got my trusty stopwatch.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.033
And here they come
down the hill.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.534
-And go right to this.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:34.467
-Ruben is in the lead.
And here comes Alan --

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:35.667
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:38.801
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That was a bad idea.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:41.000
-Oh!
-So much better!

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.634
Wow!
-That's a 360.

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:43.634
-Wow!

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:46.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.767
Whew!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:50.701
Guys, get this --
I read that Whole Foods

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:53.701
is asking suppliers
to lower their prices.

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:55.200
Yeah.
We've gotten to the point

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.000
where even Whole Foods can't
afford Whole Foods.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:01.400
Hey, I heard about a 22-year-old
basketball coach

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.667
who was fired
after she allegedly posed

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:07.300
as a 13-year-old girl and played
in a J.V. basketball game.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.567
Yep, the coach was fired,
but on the bright side,

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:12.567
she was just selected
to replace George Santos

00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:14.367
on two House committees.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.367 --> 00:06:16.434
Isn't that amazing?
[ Applause ]

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:18.734
That's not all bad.

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:20.767
Finally, everyone,
it is Tuesday.

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:23.167
It is time for "WeTweet."
Here we go, everyone.

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:26.400
-♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.200
♪♪

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.467
♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:30.801
-Welcome to "WeTweet."

00:06:30.801 --> 00:06:32.400
This is where we, as a group,

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.000
decide something
that we should post on Twitter.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.901
I'm going to show you
five different tweets,

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:38.000
and we're all going to
vote on whether

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.200
you like each one or not.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.601
You all have voting clickers
at your seats?

00:06:40.601 --> 00:06:42.667
[ Crowd cheers ]
Good.

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:46.133
You can vote for all of them,
you can vote for none of them,

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:48.100
whatever you want,
and we'll see the results live.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.634
Hopefully you vote for
all of them.

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:51.400
Higgins, Roots,
you have clickers, too?

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.701
-Got it.
-Every vote counts.

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:54.901
-Whatever tweet
gets the most likes,

00:06:54.901 --> 00:06:57.033
we're going to tweet it out
live on the show

00:06:57.033 --> 00:07:00.133
so that you can all like it
and "WeTweet" it.

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:02.767
[ Laughter ]
It's a shared experience.

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:04.100
Alright,
you guys ready for this?

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:08.033
First tweet is...

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.634
[ Light laughter ]

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:15.400
-Wow!
♪♪

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.534
-That's the joke.

00:07:16.534 --> 00:07:20.601
That's the -- No one
has phoned it in harder.

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:24.067
"I got a good name for
those things -- blueberries."

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:26.767
Wow.

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:28.534
-This might get negative.

00:07:28.534 --> 00:07:30.434
-You voted --
It's gonna be negative votes?

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:31.467
-Yeah,
I think it'll be negative.

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.834
-I think -- Wow.

00:07:33.834 --> 00:07:35.901
I mean,
it was a stunned silence.

00:07:35.901 --> 00:07:38.434
-Yeah, it was a stunned silence.

00:07:38.434 --> 00:07:40.868
-Alright, you say 50% --
less than 50%.

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:42.367
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.667
-Wow. I kind of agree with you.
Tariq, what do you think?

00:07:44.667 --> 00:07:46.567
-I'm going to agree
with Higgins on this one.

00:07:46.567 --> 00:07:49.167
-You didn't vote?
You always vote yes.

00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:51.968
-Yes, I vote yes.
-But on this one, did you?

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:54.033
-I kind of did, yeah.
-Alright.

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:56.701
He's very honest. Votes are in.
Let's see the results.

00:07:56.701 --> 00:07:57.701
[ Drumroll ]

00:07:57.701 --> 00:08:00.601
-Ooh, my God!
-Oh, yeah!

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:04.367
-Thirty-three.
-Was it that bad?

00:08:04.367 --> 00:08:06.567
That's not an original name --
blueberries.

00:08:06.567 --> 00:08:08.167
This guy kind of phoned it in
a little bit.

00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:10.434
-More like a sentence.

00:08:10.434 --> 00:08:11.567
-This next one here says...

00:08:16.267 --> 00:08:17.567
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:08:17.567 --> 00:08:20.167
There's got to be a --
-This is going to be better.

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:21.834
-He's got a Bat phone.
He's got everything.

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.133
-You can't call him?

00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:24.300
-No, he has to keep
looking out his window and go,

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.300
"Oh, not yet."

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.834
-Anybody? No.

00:08:26.834 --> 00:08:28.634
-"They need me?
No, they don't need me yet."

00:08:28.634 --> 00:08:30.567
Alright,
let's see the results here.

00:08:30.567 --> 00:08:31.834
I feel better about this one.

00:08:31.834 --> 00:08:32.968
[ Drumroll ]

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:35.000
Oh!
-Oh, wow!

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:38.734
Alright, thank you.
-Yeah.

00:08:38.734 --> 00:08:41.267
-Now I know that
your thumbs-up button works,

00:08:41.267 --> 00:08:42.567
that's good to know.

00:08:42.567 --> 00:08:44.400
I was worried for a second.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.968
Alright, this next one says...

00:08:49.734 --> 00:08:51.734
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:08:53.667 --> 00:08:55.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.901
Alright, let's see the results.

00:09:10.901 --> 00:09:12.534
[ Drumroll ]

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:14.033
Yeah, not bad.
-Oh!

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:16.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Batman.

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:18.200
Batman's still in the lead.
-Yeah.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.567
-Alright, how about this?
Next up, it says...

00:09:23.334 --> 00:09:24.400
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.634
We tried it.

00:09:26.634 --> 00:09:29.033
We tried as hard as we could.

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:31.200
Not going to work.
Not going to be a thing.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.000
-People tried.
-People tried hard.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.100
They tried with kale.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.534
Kale kind of
took off for a little bit.

00:09:35.534 --> 00:09:36.767
-Brussels sprouts took off.
-Had one or two good records.

00:09:36.767 --> 00:09:37.934
-Yeah.

00:09:37.934 --> 00:09:40.033
-Cauliflower, it ain't --
just not going to do it.

00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:42.033
Let's see the results
on this one.

00:09:42.033 --> 00:09:43.033
[ Drumroll ]

00:09:43.033 --> 00:09:45.067
Oh, wow!
-Oh, wow!

00:09:45.067 --> 00:09:46.267
No, thank you.

00:09:46.267 --> 00:09:48.634
-Some people chose
not to play at all.

00:09:48.634 --> 00:09:50.501
"I am not --
I'm not going to waste my b--

00:09:50.501 --> 00:09:51.934
my energy to type
in that button there."

00:09:51.934 --> 00:09:53.000
-Wow.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.033
-Alright,
this last one here is...

00:09:58.534 --> 00:10:00.701
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:10:00.701 --> 00:10:05.033
I feel like it's going to be --
-I like this one.

00:10:05.033 --> 00:10:06.501
-It's the Batman.

00:10:06.501 --> 00:10:08.334
-Yeah, Batman for the win.
-It's gotta be. Yeah.

00:10:08.334 --> 00:10:09.434
Alright, here we go.

00:10:09.434 --> 00:10:11.234
Let's see the results
right here.

00:10:11.234 --> 00:10:12.267
[ Drumroll ]

00:10:12.267 --> 00:10:14.167
Ooh, not bad.
-Oh!

00:10:14.167 --> 00:10:16.567
The winner is Batman!

00:10:16.567 --> 00:10:19.667
Oh, my God.
-Whoa!

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:21.167
-"...a light in the sky."

00:10:21.167 --> 00:10:23.200
I'm going to post this
during the commercial break.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.434
If you see it on your feed,
give it a like,

00:10:25.434 --> 00:10:27.467
give it a "WeTweet," and enjoy.

